    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, the Austin Waves offense is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27), who both find themselves in premium spots against right-handed pitching. **Gunnar Henderson** is our clear top play; his profile is bolstered by an elite matchup against Arrighetti, a favorable platoon split, and, critically, his ability to exploit a slow pitcher delivery to hunt stolen bases\u2014our most precious commodity. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) benefit immensely from a high-efficiency park factor and a generous matchup against Dobnak and Ginn, respectively. These secondary pieces, paired with the consistent upside of **Jacob Wilson** (71.63), provide the high-ceiling rotation necessary to contend in a 5x5 Roto environment where stolen base scarcity remains a constant pressure on roster construction.\n\nStrategic depth remains a point of emphasis for the bench, where **Josh Jung** (41.87) stood as the strongest exclusion of the day. Despite a solid base projection, **Josh Jung** fell victim to a tough matchup against Murphy, whose 2.70 xERA severely suppressed his ceiling, pushing him just below the threshold of our active starters. We are opting to bench him to preserve our limited game caps while trusting the superior matchups for **Miguel Vargas** and **Sam Antonacci**. Both **Miguel Vargas** and **Sam Antonacci** are capitalizing on a favorable encounter with Bieber; their scores (63.06 and 67.67, respectively) are driven by strong xwOBA projections and a significant SP skill edge. We remain cautious of **Heliot Ramos** (44.20), who draws a challenging start against Woo; while he remains in the lineup to ensure coverage, his sub-50 score suggests he is on a short leash should the game script turn against him.",
